  OK   this machine's TCP table attributes a loopback connection to the process that opened it (proved against this process, 586636). A same-machine client the launcher registered CAN satisfy a migration bound to its sign-in.
  OK   process start times are readable: this process (586636) started at unix 1789272258 (recorded per attestation, so a recycled process id is readable afterwards)
  NOTE binding is decided at the LOGIN server (--bind-migrations), not here. This channel logs one ATTESTED / NOT ATTESTED line per migration hello either way, so a run with binding still OFF measures whether turning it on would work.
