04:04:18.865 advertise: AUTO - each client is told the host it can actually reach:
04:04:18.865   a client on a private, loopback, link-local or CGNAT address is told the
04:04:18.865   address it reached this server on; a client on a public address is told
04:04:18.865   this box's public address, below.
04:04:18.865   public address: 203.0.113.42 (from checkip.amazonaws.com, re-checked every 10 min)
04:04:18.865   channel 0: port 8485, host decided per connection
04:04:18.865   channel 1: port 8486, host decided per connection
04:04:18.865 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
04:04:18.865   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
04:04:18.865 SET-FIELD PROBE IS ON - which by now means 'the channel answers at all'. The
04:04:18.865   flag is a misnomer kept for the launch line: without it Session::handle
04:04:18.865   returns nothing for every packet, so the migration hello goes unanswered and
04:04:18.865   the client freezes on 'Connecting...'.
04:04:18.865   With it on, this channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
04:04:18.865   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
04:04:18.865   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
04:04:18.865   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
04:04:18.866   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
04:04:18.866   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
04:04:18.866   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
04:04:18.866   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
04:04:18.866   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
